  Preamble

This license governs the use, reproduction, modification, and distribution of LicenseTrack and any Derivative Works thereof. LicenseTrack is made available as source-available software: the source code is publicly accessible, but use is subject to the conditions set out in this document.

The intent of this license is straightforward. Organisations are free to use LicenseTrack to manage their own software licenses at no cost. Individuals and organisations are free to build plugins, extensions, and integrations on top of LicenseTrack and to publish or distribute those works under their own terms, provided they are genuinely additive and do not constitute a repackaging of LicenseTrack itself. Commercial exploitation of LicenseTrack as a product or service, including offering it to third parties or incorporating it into a commercial offering, requires a separate written agreement with the Licensor.

  1. Definitions

"Software" means LicenseTrack, including all source code, documentation, configuration files, and associated materials made available under this license.

"Licensor" means Alexander Janssen, or any person or entity to whom the copyright in the Software is lawfully assigned or transferred.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this license.

"Affiliate" means any legal entity that Controls, is Controlled by, or is under common Control with You. "Control" means ownership of substantially all the assets of an entity, or the power to direct its management and policies by vote, contract, or otherwise. Control can be direct or indirect.

"Internal Use" means use of the Software solely to track, manage, and report on software licenses held by You or Your Affiliates for the operations of You and Your Affiliates, where You or an Affiliate operates the Software and the licenses being tracked belong to You or Your Affiliates.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software, or a service substantially powered by the Software, that generates revenue or other commercial benefit, including but not limited to: offering the Software as a hosted or managed service to third parties; charging fees for access to or use of the Software; and incorporating the Software into a commercial product or offering. Commercial Use does not include Internal Use permitted under Section 2.1.

"Derivative Work" means any work that is based on or derived from the Software and that reproduces or incorporates a substantial portion of the Software's source code, including modifications, forks, adaptations, and translations of the Software. A Plugin, Extension, or Integration is not a Derivative Work solely because it interfaces with or extends the Software through the Software's published API, documented extension points, import/export contracts, webhook mechanisms, or configuration mechanisms.

"Plugin, Extension, or Integration" means a standalone software component, such as a connector, extension, script, sidecar service, integration module, import/export adapter, webhook consumer, or optional capability module, that interfaces with the Software through its published API, documented extension points, import/export contracts, webhook mechanisms, or configuration mechanisms, but does not reproduce or incorporate a substantial portion of the Software's source code.

"Implementation Services" means time-limited professional services to install, configure, and deploy the Software for a client, after which the client operates the Software independently for Internal Use.

  2. Grant of License

    2.1 Internal Use

Subject to the terms of this license, the Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable license to:

use, copy, and run the Software for Internal Use;

modify the Software for Your own Internal Use, without any obligation to publish those modifications;

distribute unmodified copies of the Software to other parties, provided that such distribution includes this license in full and the recipient uses the Software solely for Internal Use.

Each recipient of an unmodified copy receives rights directly from the Licensor under this license, and You may not grant any rights in the Software beyond those expressly granted by this license.

Example: A consulting firm may use LicenseTrack to track its own internal software licenses. It may customise the Software privately, for example by adding an integration with a discovery tool, without being required to publish those changes. It may not use LicenseTrack to track its clients' licenses.

Example: A company may track any software license where that company or one of its Affiliates is the named end licensee — that is, the organisation in whose name the license was purchased and to whom the entitlement belongs. If the name of your organisation, or of a group company under common Control with it, is on the license agreement or entitlement certificate, you may manage that record in your LicenseTrack instance under Internal Use. A shared-services entity or group IT department may therefore operate a single instance covering the licenses of its parent, subsidiaries, and sister companies. You may not use LicenseTrack to track licenses belonging to, or held on behalf of, an organisation outside Your corporate group.

    2.2 Plugins, Extensions, and Integrations

You may create, publish, distribute, and commercialise Plugins, Extensions, or Integrations that extend or connect with the Software. Plugins, Extensions, and Integrations are not subject to the restrictions in Section 3 and may be released under any license terms You choose, including proprietary or commercial terms.

To qualify as a Plugin, Extension, or Integration under this license, a work must satisfy all of the following:

it does not reproduce or incorporate a substantial portion of the Software's source code;

it is genuinely additive, meaning that it extends, connects to, or automates the Software rather than replacing or repackaging its core functionality;

it does not, in combination with other components, constitute a functional equivalent of the Software offered to third parties as a service.

Example: A standalone connector that pulls discovered software from Lansweeper and pushes it into LicenseTrack via the API is a Plugin, Extension, or Integration and may be published or sold freely.

Example: An optional document-parsing sidecar that uses a documented LicenseTrack document-action extension point and returns proposed field values for user review is a Plugin, Extension, or Integration, provided it does not reproduce or incorporate a substantial portion of the Software's source code.

Example: A fork of LicenseTrack with a Lansweeper tab added directly inside the core application frontend, and distributed as a modified LicenseTrack application, is a Derivative Work and is subject to Section 3.

Example: A white-labelled copy of LicenseTrack, or a modified version of the LicenseTrack frontend that preserves the Software's core functionality and is distributed to third parties, is a Derivative Work and is subject to Section 3.

Example: A separately maintained dashboard that reads LicenseTrack data through the API and adds reporting views, without reproducing a substantial portion of the Software's source code or replacing its core functionality, may qualify as a Plugin, Extension, or Integration.

    2.3 Implementation Services

You may provide Implementation Services to a client in exchange for payment. This is permitted provided that: (a) the resulting deployment is used solely by the client for Internal Use; (b) You do not retain ongoing operational access to or control of the deployed instance after the implementation engagement concludes; and (c) You do not market or represent the engagement as a managed, hosted, or recurring service.

    2.4 Internal Hosting

An organisation may host and operate the Software on infrastructure it controls, including cloud infrastructure, as a deployment for its own Internal Use. Hosting the Software for the benefit of third parties is not permitted under this license.

