Offering the Software as a service to third parties. This includes hosted services, managed services, and software-as-a-service offerings where the Software or its functionality is made available to parties other than You.

Tracking third-party licenses. Using the Software to track, manage, or report on software licenses belonging to a third party, regardless of whether a fee is charged.

Commercial distribution of Derivative Works. Distributing, publishing, or making available a Derivative Work to third parties, whether for free or for payment, without a commercial license from the Licensor.

Incorporation into a commercial product. Incorporating the Software into a commercial product or offering that is sold, licensed, or otherwise distributed to third parties.

Sublicensing. Sublicensing the Software or granting third parties rights beyond those granted in Section 2.

Removal of notices. Removing or altering any copyright notice, license notice, or attribution statement in the Software or its documentation.

